WEBVTT

NOTE
Narration for real-run.mp4, a 1:51 cut of docs/media/demo-walkthrough.mp4 (one real run of the showcase shoot,
28 October 2026), from that file's notes. The video plays at real speed; [bracketed] times are the real time each
cut skips, read off the run clock in the trace.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
One real run on the demo shoot. I press Run QC and leave the agent to it.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.200
[10 s later] It writes a plan first, as the loop requires.

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.000
Then it checks every photo against the camera’s own brackets.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
[56 s later] The checks propose candidates, each with a confidence.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
It decides: split the laundry photo in two, put back an erased stop sign.

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
[18 s later] Every edit gets a self-check.

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.500
[9 s later] This one fails: the judge finds the restored sign cut off and soft.

8
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.000
The loop reverts it, and the agent retries with a wider mask.

9
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.500
[24 s later] The second try passes: zero pixels changed outside the mask.

10
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.400
[2 min 31 s later] QC is done: 4 min 51 s, 42 cents.

11
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.300
Three fixed and ten dismissed, each with its reason.

12
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.300
[6 s later] The editor’s finished photo had erased this stop sign.

13
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.700
Before on the left, after on the right: the sign is back, nothing else changed.

14
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.500
[5 s later] A request for the whole shoot: remove the cars and trash bins.

15
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.500
[3 min 14 s later] Three photos edited, each edit checked and passed.

16
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.000
The other seven photos say why nothing was done.

17
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.500
[17 s later] For one specific object, I shift-click it.

18
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.600
The clicks become a mask, which goes with my next message.

19
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.500
“Put the reference image on this screen.”

20
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.200
[50 s later] The first try broke the TV mount; the judge caught it.

21
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.700
A tighter, screen-only mask passed on the second try.

22
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:34.500
The customer’s photo is on the screen; the mount and the wall are unchanged.

23
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:40.000
[2 min 8 s later] I approve the photos and build the reel.

24
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.500
The agent labels the rooms, orders them and renders a 9:16 listing reel.

25
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:51.300
Twenty-four seconds, eight photos, ready to post.
